@startuml run-states
' DOC-9. The status of a run, as engine/scheduler.py (status) and model/history.py (_status) say it
' from the events alone. A finished run has an outcome (RunOutcome): SUCCEEDED, GOAL_NOT_REACHED,
' FAILED, CANCELLED, COMPENSATED or COMPENSATION_FAILED.
skinparam shadowing false

state CREATED
state RUNNING
state WAITING
state COMPENSATING
state FINISHED

[*] --> CREATED

CREATED --> RUNNING : RUN_STARTED
CREATED --> FINISHED : cancelled before the start

RUNNING --> WAITING : a step waits for an answer, or one is UNCERTAIN
WAITING --> RUNNING : the answer came, or a person resolved the step
RUNNING --> COMPENSATING : every step is final and a step failed under on_failure compensate
COMPENSATING --> WAITING : an undo is UNCERTAIN and no other runs
WAITING --> COMPENSATING : the person resolves the undo
RUNNING --> FINISHED : every step is final; the outcome is set
WAITING --> FINISHED : the time limit or a cancel ends the last step
COMPENSATING --> FINISHED : every undo is final (COMPENSATED or COMPENSATION_FAILED)

FINISHED --> [*]
@enduml
